  "notes": "I was Black in a club rapid game and wanted to test an old line I had read about. Looking back, my problem was not one bad move but a plan: I gave up my light-squared bishop early and then kept my king in the centre while my opponent developed with tempo. <script>alert('xss')</script> is what a careless page would run here.\n\nThe lesson I took from this game is simple: when you trade your bishop for a knight in the opening, you owe your position development, not pawn grabs."
